## Code review and class-per-file refactor proposal

Context: First code review of the 0.9.0 branch, followed by an analysis of
how to move to one class per file with small, single-purpose classes.
Proposal only: no application code was changed. Baseline: 21 classes
> 800 LOC, 29 files with several public classes, 41 `{"success": False}`
envelopes, 746 `except Exception`, and delegating facades in
`SettingsService` (107/120 methods), `DigitalTwin` (76/84) and
`GraphEngineSettings` (26/36). Found a duplicate method pair in
`CohortBuilder` (first definitions unreachable).

Changes:

1. .planning/class-per-file-refactor/PLAN.md
   New plan: review findings (rule compliance, duplication, dead code,
   session sample, tests), target design rules, phased Fowler refactorings
   (guardrails, quick file splits, agent Template Method base, Remove Middle
   Man, god-class decompositions, routes/schemas, module functions to
   classes), risks and open decisions.

