## Add architecture guardrails, start class-per-file split, update rules and skills

Context: Phase 0 and the first part of phase 1 of
`.planning/class-per-file-refactor/PLAN.md`, following the decisions
taken today (records grouped by aggregate root, facades and shims removed
outright, start with guardrails and quick wins). The project rules and
skills now state the target shape and that the simplest code is always
the best. No behaviour change: classes were moved verbatim and every
importer (src and tests) was updated; no shim modules were left behind.

Changes:

1. tests/units/architecture/ (new)
   AST guardrails: one public class per file + filename match, class/method
   size ceilings (800/100 LOC), silent redefinitions (F811), back/objects
   re-exports. Known offenders frozen in a shrink-only baseline.json;
   ratchet.py tightens it and follows entries moved without growing.
