## Redirect unloaded workspace pages to Home
================================================================================

Context:
Visiting Domain, Ontology, Mapping, or Knowledge Graph with no domain in
session rendered an empty workspace (hidden L2 rail, placeholder NewDomain).
Those HTML routes now 303 to Home immediately. Settings, About, and Home stay
reachable without a domain. Closing a domain still navigates Home; creating a
new domain still stays on the current page until the name is saved.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/domain/WorkspacePresence.py (new)
   Loaded-session check mirroring navbar.js domainIsLoaded (custom name or
   ontology/mapping content).
2. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   home_redirect_if_unloaded() returns a 303 to /.
3. src/front/routes/{domain,ontology,mapping,dtwin}.py
   Workspace page GET handlers run the guard before rendering (graphless
   Mapping/KG fallback still applies after a domain is loaded).
4. tests/units/front/test_unloaded_workspace_redirect.py (new)
   Source contract plus HTTP 303/200 for unloaded vs named sessions.
5. tests/units/domain/test_domain_service.py, tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py,
   tests/units/api/test_routes.py
   Presence unit tests; HTML render helpers seed a named domain.
6. docs/user-guide.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/sphinx/api/app.objects.domain.rst
   Document the redirect and autodoc the new class.
7. src/back/objects/domain/__init__.py
   Re-export WorkspacePresence.

