## Merge PR #193 (MCP client examples) and add tests for it
================================================================================

Context:
PR #193 (generic MCP client, benchmark harness, client optimization guide) was
squash-merged into 0.9.0 as 24732739. The two example scripts had no tests.
Writing them showed that `mcp_client.py --no-opt-tools` was parsed but never
used: the curated tool descriptions (OPT 1) could not be switched off, while
`mcp_bench.py` kept its own copy of the fallback logic.

Changes:
1. examples/mcp_client.py
   `tools_to_openai(..., curated=True)` switch; `ask(..., opt_tools=True)` and
   the CLI (`--no-opt-tools`, also for `--list`) honour it.
2. examples/mcp_bench.py
   Baseline tool descriptions come from `tools_to_openai(curated=False)`
   instead of a duplicated inline fallback.
3. tests/units/examples/ (new: conftest.py, _fakes.py, 2 test files, 55 tests)
   - test_mcp_client_example.py: curated descriptions must cover exactly the
     server's `@mcp.tool` functions (drift guard) and the size tables only name
     real tools; domain warm-up and system prompt; entity-block summarization
     run against the server's real `_format_graphql_response` output (keeps the
     matching entity, tie order, zero-score guard, per-section summaries);
     result caps; agent loop (reasoning blocks stripped, compression and OPT 1
     switches, 12-round limit); MCP streamable-HTTP parsing (SSE and JSON,
     session id reuse, JSON-RPC errors, initialize warning) via
     httpx.MockTransport; Databricks LLM request shape; CLI token retrieval.
   - test_mcp_bench_example.py: per-round tokens and tool timings, raw size
     measured before compression, baseline switches reach the LLM request,
     error and max-round capture, tool stats and report hints.

Modified files:
